# Prestium Keys (Gajim's OpenPGP key): a session bus with one name only, GnuPG's passphrase prompter
# (compatibility audit: with no bus at all, its gpg-agent's pinentry could not show a prompt, so
# generating a protected key, a backup's new passphrase, importing from Kleopatra with an added user
# ID and editing a protected key all failed). It holds Gajim's private key; its own file dialogs
# (GTK 3, in the process) only see what its AppArmor profile allows.
include pinentry
